Fail the 6-hourly scan when a distributor PO parses but produces zero events.

Approved by JD 2026-08-02. Verified against the full suite (97 passed).

WHY
---
A PO PDF that parses but emits no events is a wiring gap, not a blip: the
order is real, it is sitting in the inbox, and on_order stays wrong until
someone adds the ship-to DC or the item code. Today the only trace is a
string in `errors`, and the cron still exits 0 -- so the run reads "OK".

That hid three separate drops:

  US Foods Houston      PO 305202B2  1120 cs  2 days / 5 runs
  US Foods Aurora       PO 275346     168 cs  since 2026-07-21
  US Foods Bensenville  PO 843051     391 cs  since 2026-02-05

Everything parsed successfully is applied BEFORE the non-zero exit, and the
apply path is idempotent (PO-revision guard in sync_inventory), so failing
the run loses nothing and the next run re-processes safely.

APPLY
-----
    git apply patches/0001-fail-cron-on-dropped-po.patch
    python -m pytest -q
    python scripts/safe_push.py
    git add -A && git commit -m 'Fail the cron when a PO parses to zero events' && git push

Render's cron-failure notification then fires on the next drop instead of the
run reading "OK".

